--TEST--
`Core\Sse->receive` throws a `LogicError` in a request that answers with its own events, and names the member — `rule:concurrency/two-doors-one-isolate`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Sse::receive
// A request that opened its stream with `Core\Sse::stream` ends with its own
// events, so nothing published could reach it. `null` here would read as "the
// stream is over" and end a loop for a reason that was never true, so the
// wait is refused instead.
var $refused = "";
try {
    Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
        var $sse = Core\Sse::stream();
        $sse->receive();
    });
} catch (LogicError $caught) {
    $refused = $caught->message;
}
echo Core\Str::contains($refused, "Core\\Sse::receive") ? "refused by name" : $refused, "\n";
--EXPECT--
refused by name
